From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:20:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] configure: use the host python and meson instead of a venv

qemu 11.1.2 port of
meta-xt-qemu/recipes-qemu/qemu/qemu/0114-configure-use-the-host-python-and-meson-not-a-venv.patch;
that patch's description has the reasoning and the measurements.

Ported: Same host python/mkvenv replacement; qemu 11.1.2's configure
computes the venv meson in a new block (get_pwd, EXESUF, Haiku), so
instead of replacing that line the port overrides meson with the host
one right after it.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific; see the oe-core originals]
---
 configure | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 6ddfe4b53..5cbdccb03 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -937,14 +937,14 @@ python="$(command -v "$python")"
 echo "python determined to be '$python'"
 echo "python version: $($python --version)"
 
-python="$($python -B "${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py" create pyvenv)"
+python=python3
 if test "$?" -ne 0 ; then
     error_exit "python venv creation failed"
 fi
 
 # Suppress writing compiled files
 python="$python -B"
-mkvenv="$python ${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py"
+mkvenv=true
 
 # Finish preparing the virtual environment using vendored .whl files.
 # Even if PyPI is allowed, we disallow it here to force installation
@@ -978,6 +978,9 @@ if test "$host_os" = "haiku" && test ! -e "$meson" ; then
     meson="$(cd pyvenv/non-packaged/bin; get_pwd)/meson"
 fi
 
+# Yocto (0114): use the host meson from PATH, not the venv one; mkvenv is disabled above.
+meson=$(command -v meson)
+
 mkvenv_online_flag=""
 if test "$download" = "enabled" ; then
     mkvenv_online_flag=" --online"
